{
  "$comment": [
    "What scripts/site-crops.mjs cuts out of the captures, and how. Run it with --sources <folder of captures>;",
    "scripts/site-shots/shoot makes the captures and runs it (site/README.md, \"Captures\").",
    "The windows are HangarAI 3.0 drawn headless by hangar-app's ignored test marketing::pictures, on its demo",
    "workspace: a 1440 x 900 window at scale 2, so 2880 x 1800 px (panes: 1520 x 900; chatm, chatml: 760 x 900).",
    "rect: [x, y, width, height] in capture pixels (scale 1: one capture pixel per unit).",
    "widths: the files written, img/<name>-<width>.avif and .webp; the page's srcset follows them.",
    "fade: pixels over which an edge the crop cuts through fades to that edge's own colour.",
    "Names ending in -m are the phone crops: one panel, drawn near its real size on a phone.",
    "hero-m, hero-light-m: the conversation of « Chat + team », the tiles stacked beside it in a 760 px window.",
    "model, model-m: the 3D preview, which the test's software renderer does not draw; still the 2.2 capture.",
    "Names starting with mobile- are Hangar Mobile itself, in its mock mode (scripts/site-shots/mobile.mjs): whole screens,",
    "390 x 844 at scale 2 with an iPhone's safe areas, the PC and a workspace renamed; the page draws the phone.",
    "cloud, cloud-light: the Cloud space at work as 3.0 has it (a Cloud Builds machine, a hosted node, a share link, images and dictation); on no page now.",
    "cloud-builds, cloud-builds-light: Cloud Builds' price sheet with its machine picker (the catalog's classes, an RTX 4090 picked), cut to the sheet; the home's cloud pillar and the pricing page's Pro or Max.",
    "license, license-light: Settings › License; plans, plans-light: the plans from a trial's badge; the pricing page.",
    "pages: the pages whose data-crop tags the script fills, each with its way to img/."
  ],
  "scale": 1,
  "out": ".",
  "pages": [
    {
      "page": "../index.html",
      "href": "img/"
    },
    {
      "page": "../pricing/index.html",
      "href": "../img/"
    }
  ],
  "formats": {
    "avif": {
      "quality": 62,
      "speed": 4
    },
    "webp": {
      "quality": 82,
      "method": 6
    }
  },
